From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Cui <bh@bugs.cc>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 01:37:44 -0400
Subject: feat: report, check, and upgrade the distribution this install came
 from

`__version__`, the PyPI update check, and `cswap upgrade` all hard-code the
`claude-swap` distribution. A repackaging that ships the same `claude_swap`
module under another distribution name (aswap: upstream plus a patch series,
command `aswap`) then breaks in three ways: importing the package raises
PackageNotFoundError for `claude-swap`, every run compares aswap's version
against claude-swap's PyPI release and nags about an "update", and `upgrade`
runs `uv tool upgrade claude-swap`, which reinstalls the other project.

A new `claude_swap.distribution` module answers which distribution provides
the `claude_swap` package from the installed metadata
(`importlib.metadata.packages_distributions`), preferring a repackaging over
upstream when both are present. `__version__` reads that distribution's
version, the update check queries its PyPI project and names it in the
message, and the self-upgrade upgrades it. The command shown in hints is
`cswap` for upstream and the distribution name otherwise. Upstream installs
behave exactly as before.

